<template>
    <heading>Select/Create Project Dialog</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>dialog</li>
        <li>project selection</li>
        <li>project creation</li>
        <li>modal</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>The dialog defaults to Local directory. Remote URL reveals one project-directory URL field; there is no root-filename field. The final directory name is the root article filename, just as with local projects. Remote Create is disabled until server-side creation is defined; the local Create button remains unwired.</p>
        <p>Select dispatches the location and URL snapshot using <code>dispatchImmediate</code>. The generator primes its async work immediately, preserving local picker user activation. Required URL validation runs before dispatch; storage validates directory URL shape and the model validates the project filename convention.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>SelectCreateProject</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
<template id="SelectCreateProject">
    <style>
        .SelectCreateProject h2 { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.25rem; }
        .SelectCreateProject fieldset { border: 0; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
        .SelectCreateProject legend { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
        .SelectCreateProject .locations { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
        .SelectCreateProject .remote-url { display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
        .SelectCreateProject input[type="url"] {
            display: block; box-sizing: border-box; width: 100%; margin-top: 0.5rem;
            padding: 0.5rem; font: inherit;
        }
        .SelectCreateProject .dialog-buttons {
            display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem;
        }
        .SelectCreateProject [hidden] { display: none; }
    </style>
    <dialog id="SelectCreateProject-dialog" class="SelectCreateProject"
            aria-labelledby="SelectCreateProject-title">
        <h2 id="SelectCreateProject-title">Select or Create a Project</h2>
        <fieldset>
            <legend>Project location</legend>
            <div class="locations">
                <label><input id="SelectCreateProject-Local" type="radio"
                    name="project-location" value="local" checked> Local directory</label>
                <label><input id="SelectCreateProject-Remote" type="radio"
                    name="project-location" value="remote"> Remote URL</label>
            </div>
        </fieldset>
        <p id="SelectCreateProject-LocalInfo">Select an existing project directory or create a new one on this computer.</p>
        <label id="SelectCreateProject-RemoteField" class="remote-url" hidden>
            Project directory URL
            <input id="SelectCreateProject-URL" type="url" required spellcheck="false"
                placeholder="https://example.com/projects/demo.lp5/">
        </label>
        <div class="dialog-buttons">
            <button id="SelectCreateProject-Create" type="button">Create…</button>
            <button id="SelectCreateProject-Select" type="button" autofocus>Select…</button>
        </div>
        <script>
            const local = elementByID["SelectCreateProject-Local"];
            const remote = elementByID["SelectCreateProject-Remote"];
            const url = elementByID["SelectCreateProject-URL"];
            const select = elementByID["SelectCreateProject-Select"];
            function updateLocation() {
                elementByID["SelectCreateProject-LocalInfo"].hidden = remote.checked;
                elementByID["SelectCreateProject-RemoteField"].hidden = !remote.checked;
                elementByID["SelectCreateProject-Create"].disabled = remote.checked;
                select.textContent = remote.checked ? "Select" : "Select…";
            }
            local.addEventListener("change", updateLocation);
            remote.addEventListener("change", updateLocation);
            select.addEventListener("click", () => {
                if (remote.checked && !url.reportValidity()) return;
                window.LP5.controller.dispatchImmediate({
                    name: "SelectProject", location: remote.checked ? "remote" : "local",
                    url: remote.checked ? url.value.trim() : undefined
                });
            });
            return elementByID["SelectCreateProject-dialog"];
        </script>
    </dialog>
</template>
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
